.TH "YAMLR-INSTALL" "1" "November 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
\fBAutomated CI/CD Workflow & Git Hook Installer\fR
.PP
The \fByamlr install\fR command installs automated Yamlr enforcement integrations directly into your Git workspace.
.PP
---
.PP
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
.RS
yamlr install {hook|action} [flags]
.RE
.fi
---
.PP
.SH "TARGETS"
.SS "1. `hook`"
Installs a zero-latency Git pre-commit hook into \fB.git/hooks/pre-commit\fR.
.PP
.nf
.RS
yamlr install hook
.RE
.fi
Every commit will automatically trigger a sub-50ms audit across staged manifests, preventing invalid YAML and schema regressions from entering git history.
.PP
.SS "2. `action`"
Generates an official GitHub Actions workflow template at \fB.github/workflows/yamlr-safety.yml\fR.
.PP
.nf
.RS
yamlr install action
.RE
.fi
Automatically audits pull requests, generates SARIF reports for the GitHub Code Scanning tab, and blocks merges on critical defect thresholds.
.PP
---
.PP
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.nf
.RS
# Protect every local commit with a pre-commit guard
yamlr install hook

# Add Yamlr auditing to your GitHub Actions CI pipeline
yamlr install action
.RE
.fi
